    "solution": "Use the minor out-spec of round pin terminal @ dim 3:0.0607-0.0608(spec is 0.0609-0.0616) for production.\nThe function of the pin is to act as a connector by staking it with the coil terminal during the molding process. We tested this by taking 16 pieces of the pin terminal, assembling and staking them to the coil terminals, and then molding them as below\nAssemble the pin terminals and stake them to the coil terminals. All samples are firmly attached to the coil terminals, with no damage, and all samples passed visual inspections.\nMolding process: All samples fit well with the mold, and there is no molding flash on the terminal round pin. Visual inspection after molding shows that all samples passed as below\nWe are concerned about the impact of the undersized pin on the end user, so we worked with James, who confirmed that we can accept these pins.\nConclusion: We can accept these pin terminals of this batch for production.",
    "actions": "1. Discuss with Team for out-of-spec round pin terminal.\nTake 16pcs of the terminal round pin, assemble them to coil terminal, and then pass them through the molding for checking.\n3. Work with the vendor to implement corrective and preventive actions for the issue.\n4. Discuss with DC Engineering about the undersized pin terminal\n5. Issue DEV",
